# npm auth for publishing @ic402/client + @ic402/mcp to the public registry.
#
# PER-REPO token in a gitignored `.npmrc`, so ic402 and sibling repos (e.g. engramx) each publish
# with their OWN token — no shared global ~/.npmrc token needed.
#
# pnpm does NOT expand ${ENV_VARS} in a project .npmrc auth line (a deliberate security measure:
# it assumes a project .npmrc could be committed and leak the token). So the token must be a
# LITERAL value here — which is safe because `.npmrc` is gitignored and never leaves your machine.
#
# Create your local .npmrc the pnpm-native way (writes the file for you):
#
#   pnpm config set "//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken" npm_xxxxxxxxxxxx --location project
#
# ...or `cp .npmrc.example .npmrc` and paste your token below. Use an npm *automation* token
# (revocable). `mops publish` uses separate mops auth, not this token.
//registry.npmjs.org/:_authToken=npm_REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_AUTOMATION_TOKEN
